+  // receiver class) and already has a frameless body, this module imports
+  // that body as a function and calls it itself: the class check inline, the
+  // arguments stored where its locals expect them, no C at all. A frameless
+  // body can never reach the GC or a safepoint, so the caller's operand stack
+  // stays in wasm locals -- no spill, no reload. Anything else (another
+  // class, a null receiver, the stack near its end, a body that asks to be
+  // retried) takes the ordinary zwc_invoke path below, which starts from
